cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PicTrace in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PicTrace: Open-source Reverse Image Provenance Search Aggregator"
type: software
authors:
  - name: xiaoanping-101
    website: "https://github.com/xiaoanping-101"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/xiaoanping-101/pictrace"
    description: "Repository URL"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiaoanping-101/pictrace"
abstract: >-
  PicTrace (溯图) is an open-source, zero-dependency web app for image
  provenance: load an image once and search it across major reverse-image
  engines (Google Lens, Yandex, Bing, TinEye, Baidu, Sogou, SauceNAO,
  IQDB, ...), with in-browser EXIF forensics, perceptual hashes
  (aHash/dHash/pHash), an optional on-device CLIP ViT-B/32 model that
  recognizes image content type (zero-shot) and powers similar-content
  discovery — the server directly fetches real URLs of similar images,
  related videos, articles and wiki entries from keyless public sources —
  plus WeChat-article / video / social classification and citation-ready
  Markdown reporting.
keywords:
  - reverse-image-search
  - image-provenance
  - osint
  - image-forensics
  - perceptual-hash
  - search-aggregator
license: MIT
version: 1.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
